{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794855694,"nonce":"urzEHYraDm6w6T4CLWmc8xefZOU=","target":"745472ef4f73cdfe0f7be9e56ced9a0c324257c8ade6440bbd7d2ec1fb3da526","message":"## Parent\n\nSpec: b202902 (Light Cycle stepped bands and ECharts chart overhaul)\n\n## What to build\n\nThe flagship slice: Target Bands step between day and night. Core expands a light-state timeline for the Chart window — the bound light entity's real on/off history wins wherever it has in-window readings; the grow's Light Cycle (lights-on time + per-phase hours via the existing phase spans in the grow's timezone) fills gaps and the whole window when unbound; neither yields a single band as today. The band builder emits (phase, lights-on/off) segments using the day and night presets, merging identical neighbours; drying and curing stay single-band. The backend history endpoint emits the split segments and fixes the humidity band at the root — computed from the actual temperature series with the day/night leaf offsets — and VPD arrives clamped. The option-builder renders the stepped bands on temperature, humidity, VPD, and CO₂ (night CO₂ = ambient band). Degraded (snapshot-only) mode keeps working.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On a grow with a Light Cycle set and no light bound: bands visibly step day/night per schedule and phase\n- [ ] With a light entity bound: band steps follow real on/off history, including timer overrides\n- [ ] Humidity band sits at science-correct levels (temperature-driven, no humidity-as-temperature input)\n- [ ] Night VPD computed with the night leaf offset; VPD never negative on any chart\n- [ ] Sensor-outage degraded mode still renders\n- [ ] Tests green across the four seams: core expansion/stepping, backend segments, option-builder, e2e\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- 03 3cadef8 (Environment charts on ECharts)\n- 05 1d57bbb (Light Cycle setting on the grow)\n- 06 5fecf48 (Night presets and VPD clamp in core)","files":null}]}